Falsifies `system_tests::user::running_space_tests::a_second_bind_of_a_bound_space_is_refused`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect: the registry stops refusing a bind of a space already bound, the amendment (b) of
§249 (a running address space stays nameable) undone. A space's name survives `CONFIGURE` now, so a second capability reaches a second bind,
and two threads share one space, which §105 (`std::thread::spawn` stays declined) declines.

Expected to fail: the `WrongObject` assertion, which gets `Ok(0)`.

